WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Open the landing page. Use the capability map to choose the browser workspace or the
Python catalogue. A configured link or button click is not proof of generation.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Open Drawing catalogue. Choose a configuration by foundation and superstructure. Read
its reference-page mapping. Do not assume the browser renderer supports every Python
configuration.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:48.000
In Variables & layout, set skew_deg to 25 and inspect the comparison table. A value of
35 is outside the current 0–30 degree range. The Python resolver must still check
dependent dimensions and engineering constraints.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Paper and orientation control PNG export when the render-media CLI patch is installed.
Proposed CAD scale does not create paper-space viewports or change DXF geometry. Choose
scale for readability and inspect every view.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Save the scenario, open Saved scenarios and use Load & compare. Export a JSON backup
before moving devices or clearing browser data. Imported scenarios need review and a
Python dry run before generation.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Inspect the local generator help for supported flags. Run the prepared dry run first.
When it succeeds, run generation deliberately and retain output paths, resolved inputs
and exit codes. Baseline runs can overwrite the existing corpus.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Open generated DXF and rendered sheets alongside GENERAL ARRANGEMENT DRAWINGS.pdf.
Compare span arrangement, levels, skew, foundations, dimensions, notes, title block and
scales. Record each discrepancy as a bug or enrichment task; perfect fidelity remains
unverified.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Confirm units, datum, slope direction, parameter names and error handling across
integrations. For the existing frontend Netlify setup, verify base frontend, build npm
run build and publish dist. Deploying static pages does not deploy a Python backend.